meta {
  name: List Notes
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notes?entityType=TRUCK&entityId={{truckId}}&page=1&pageSize=20&includeReplies=false
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  entityType: TRUCK
  entityId: {{truckId}}
  page: 1
  pageSize: 20
  includeReplies: false
  ~torgId: {{torgId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Lists the caller's torg's top-level notes on an entity, newest first (`NoteResource.listNotes`,
  service `NoteService.listNotes`). Same roles as "Create Note".

  Query: `entityType` and `entityId` are required. `page` is 1-based (default 1), `pageSize` defaults to
  20 and is capped at 100. `torgId` is required for VAHN_ADMIN and ignored for everyone else.

  With `includeReplies=false` each note carries only `replyCount` (live replies at any depth). With
  `includeReplies=true` each note also has `replies`: its direct replies, oldest first, each with their
  own `replies`.

  Response `data`: `{ data: [note...], page, pageSize, total, hasMore, lastId, unread }`. `lastId` is
  always null here.

  Read status: `unread` is true when someone else added a live note (top-level or reply) since the
  caller last listed this entity's notes. Listing then marks everything read, so a second call returns
  `unread: false` until someone adds a note. The caller's own notes never make anything unread.
  VAHN_ADMIN views aren't recorded and always get `unread: false`. "Get Note" doesn't change read status.

  A deleted note is listed only while it still has live replies; it then has `deleted: true` and
  `content`/`author` null.

  400 for a missing/unknown `entityType`, a missing `entityId`, bad paging, or a truck the caller can't
  see.
}
